    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 254\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 3228, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to allowing\n      two  automatic free transfers for riders using pay-per-ride Metro-\n      cards\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would  require  the  Metropolitan  Transportation  Authority\n(MTA)  to  provide two automatic free transfers for riders between local\nbus and subway rides, or between local  bus  rides,  provided  that  the\noriginal ticket was purchased no more than two hours ago.\n\n  The  MTA  currently allows one free transfer from local bus-to-subway,\nsubway-to-local bus, or local bus-to-local bus within two hours  of  the\ntime  the  ticket was purchased. The MTA also offers an \"unlimited ride\"\nMetrocard for purchase. Multiple free transfers can be made  with  these\nweekly  and  monthly unlimited ride cards, and more than half of the MTA\ncustomers already use these unlimited  ride  cards.  Moreover,  the  MTA\nestimates  it would cost approximately $40 million annually to provide a\nsecond free transfer, yet the bill  does  not  provide  any  funding  to\naccount  for this expense. Such funding decisions should be addressed in\nthe context of the State budget negotiations. For these  reasons,  I  am\ncompelled to veto this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
